      "output_preview": "## Data Models Phase \u2014 Complete\n\n### What was accomplished\n\n**`team-test/models.py`** \u2014 Production-ready data models for the Python task management CLI tool:\n\n- **`Priority` enum** (`str` mixin): `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `CRITICAL` with numeric `.weight` property for sorting and case-insensitive `from_string()` factory.\n- **`Status` enum** (`str` mixin): `TODO`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `DONE`, `CANCELLED` with `.is_terminal` property and case-insensitive `from_string()` factory.\n- **`Task` dataclass**: Full-featured task entity with:\n  - Fields: `id` (UUID4), `title`, `description`, `priority`, `status`, `due_date`, `tags`, `created_at`, `updated_at`\n  - `__post_init__` validation (empty title, enum coercion, date format, tag normalisation/deduplication)\n  - `update(**kwargs)` for partial field updates with `updated_at` refresh\n  - `mark_done()` / `mark_cancelled()` convenience methods\n  - `is_overdue` property (respects terminal status)\n  - `short_id` property (first 8 chars of UUID)\n  - Full serialisation: `to_dict()`, `from_dict()`, `to_json()`, `from_json()`\n- **`TaskList`** collection class:\n  - CRUD: `add()`, `get_by_id()`, `get_by_short_id()`, `remove()`, `update()`\n  - Filtering: `filter_by_status()`, `filter_by_priority()`, `filter_by_tag()`, `filter_overdue()`, `search()`\n  - Sorting: `sorted_by_priority()`, `sorted_by_due_date()`, `sorted_by_created_at()`\n  - Serialisation: `to_dict()`, `from_dict()`, `to_json()`, `from_json()`\n  - `summary()` returning per-status counts + total\n  - `__len__`, `__iter__`, `__repr__`\n\n**`team-test/test_models.py`** \u2014 Comprehensive test suite:\n- **98 tests, all passing** (pytest 9.0.2, Python 3.14.2)\n- Covers: Priority, Status, Task construction/validation, Task update, is_overdue, serialisation roundtrips, TaskList CRUD, filtering, sorting, serialisation, summary, and a full end-to-end workflow integration test\n- Zero warnings (fixed `datetime.utcnow()` \u2192 `datetime.now(tz=timezone.utc)` for Python 3.14 compatibility)",
